                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d49607c-434b-489b-bcb4-b8dddf0f316c",
                                "sense_id": "ead226fa-8132-3a15-a602-dd856bdb7eb0",
                                "text": "An example where a relatively old case of phonetic dissimilation has been artificially undone in the spelling is English colonel, whose standard pronunciation is /kɝnəl/ (with the r sound) in North-American English, or /kɜːnəl/ in RP. It was formerly spelt coronel and is a borrowing from French coronel, which arose as a result of dissimilation from Italian colonnello."
